# The bats files that drive tacctl only through its command line, run against
# the Go binary with 'TACCTL_IMPL=go make test-blackbox' (docs/plans/go-rewrite.md
# 2.2). One path per line; '#' starts a comment. A file followed by
# '# go-after: <work package>' runs only in bash mode until that package has
# cut its commands over. A file followed by '# go-tags: <tag> [<tag>...]' runs
# in full in bash mode and, in go mode, only its tests tagged with one of those
# tags (characterisation.bats: the cutover:<package> tags of the packages done
# so far). Tests tagged 'bash-only' (# bats test_tags=bash-only) are skipped in
# go mode. Packages that cut commands over add the files they make pass.
tests/integration/backup.bats
tests/integration/config_linux.bats
tests/integration/config_metrics_sudoers.bats
tests/integration/config_mgmt_acl.bats
tests/integration/config_radius.bats
tests/integration/config_render.bats
tests/integration/config_setters.bats
tests/integration/config_templates.bats
tests/integration/group_crud.bats
tests/integration/group_edit_commands.bats
tests/integration/host.bats
tests/integration/listeners.bats
tests/integration/prompts_closed_stdin.bats
# 'backend enable|disable radius' and the CLI through the binary; the RADIUS
# lifecycle phases through '_phase'; its bash-only tests drive bash internals
# (WP3.3c).
tests/integration/radius.bats
tests/integration/scope_auth_method.bats
tests/integration/scope_crud.bats
tests/integration/scope_prefixes_secret.bats
tests/integration/scope_protocols.bats
tests/integration/scope_vendor_attrs.bats
tests/integration/status_and_scope_lookup.bats
tests/integration/store_mutations.bats
tests/integration/store_cli.bats
tests/integration/tiers.bats
# White-box in its setup (it drives the unit phases of install/upgrade as bash
# functions); its CLI tests run the binary (WP2.4c).
tests/integration/units_convert.bats
# White-box in their setup (state_migrate, config_sync_existing,
# upgrade_store_flip, install_seed_config and the legacy migrations run as
# bash functions; their Go ports are internal/lifecycle's tests); 'store
# rollback' and every other command line run the binary (WP3.3a).
tests/integration/upgrade_store_flip.bats
tests/integration/migrate_dead_command_matches.bats
tests/integration/migrate_exec_service_name.bats
tests/e2e/install_seed.bats
tests/integration/user_crud.bats
tests/integration/user_lifecycle.bats
tests/e2e/log.bats
tests/e2e/smoke.bats
# Its tests source the bash library with a stand-in backend (internal/backend's
# faketest is the Go side); the ones tagged cutover:wp2-4d drive the command
# line with the shipped backends (WP2.4d).
tests/integration/backend_cli.bats  # go-tags: cutover:wp2-4d
# Pins the CLI behaviour of verbs no other test covers (WP0.2): against Go, the
# sections of the packages cut over so far; whole once WP3.3d is done.
tests/integration/characterisation.bats  # go-tags: cutover:wp0-1 cutover:wp2-4a cutover:wp2-4b cutover:wp2-4c cutover:wp2-4d cutover:wp3-1 cutover:wp3-2
